ents":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6146583031","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/78#issuecomment-6146583031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/78","id":6146583031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbl1p9w","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T13:24:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T13:24:57Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 85/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **MEDIUM · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Hardcoded secret value embedded in Terraform local in source-controlled file**\n  - Category rationale: A string value labelled 'secret' is hardcoded as a Terraform local in source-controlled code. Even when the value is asserted to be non-functional, the pattern introduces a concrete risk: (1) the assertion cannot be verified by automated tooling or reviewers without out-of-band validation; (2) the pattern normalises embedding secrets in IaC, increasing the likelihood that a real credential is introduced in the same way; (3) the value will appear in Terraform state and any plan/apply output stored by Terraform Cloud, expanding its exposure surface regardless of its actual validity.\n  - Evidence: terraform/secret.tf — locals block: `tc09_dummy_secret = \"PROM06-FAKE-SECRET-NOT-VALID-12345\"`. The resource name and local name both contain the word 'secret', and the comment 'This is NOT a real credential' and 'Do not deploy this configuration' are the only controls preventing accidental use or replication.\n  - Analysis: terraform/secret.tf defines a Terraform local named 'tc09_dummy_secret' with the plaintext string value 'PROM06-FAKE-SECRET-NOT-VALID-12345'. The file comment states this is a research test only and not a real credential, and instructs not to deploy the configuration. However, the value is committed to source control as a literal string inside a locals block. Secret-scanning tools cannot distinguish a 'fake' secret from a real one based solely on the comment, and the value will be persisted in Terraform state if the configuration is ever applied. The pattern itself is a security weakness independent of the current validity of the credential.\n  - Impact: If the value is or becomes a real credential, or if a developer copies this pattern for a genuine secret, the credential is exposed in version control history, Terraform Cloud plan/apply logs, and Terraform state storage. Rotation or revocation after discovery is operationally costly. Secret-scanning suppression based on comment assertions is not a reliable control.\n  - Recommendation: Remove the hardcoded value from source control entirely. If a placeholder or test fixture is genuinely needed for the research case, reference a secret via a Terraform variable with sensitive = true and supply the value through an environment variable or a secrets manager (e.g., Azure Key Vault data source), never as a literal string in a locals block. If the file exists solely to document a test scenario, remove the locals block and keep only the comment, or delete the file.\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6146583031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"ht